x86_64-linux  cxx1 writes the C1 and D1 forms of the implicit constructors and destructors of `Both`, `Poly`, `Derived` and `Holder`, where clang emits only the C2 and D2 a use asks for (docs/CONFORMANCE.md, "An inline member function is a strong symbol"). Every special member the program writes is defined out of line, and these four classes' are the compiler's, which have no out-of-line form - running them is the point of the case.
arm64-darwin  the same rule for `Poly`, whose constructor and destructor clang emits only as the C2 and D2 `Derived` calls, `alone` being built directly here all the same.
